# v1.2 (S12): four rotations + Auto. The Kobo build has the sensor off;
# here a pretend sensor shows Auto, then the manual choices.
# On the Forma a quarter turn clockwise gives Landscape inverted (R270,
# decision in 766168f), so ccw is Landscape and cw is Landscape inverted.
copy-notes tests/test-notes/_test
expect-rotation Portrait
expect-orientation-status Auto (no sensor) — Portrait
tap-on Options
shot v1.2-options-auto-no-sensor
tap-on Close
sensor on
expect-orientation-status Auto — Portrait
tilt ccw
wait 300
expect-rotation Portrait
wait 600
expect-rotation Landscape
shot v1.2-auto-landscape
tilt 180
wait 900
expect-rotation Portrait inverted
shot v1.2-auto-portrait-inverted
tilt cw
wait 900
expect-rotation Landscape inverted
shot v1.2-auto-landscape-inverted
tap-on Options
shot v1.2-options-auto-landscape-inverted
tap-on Orientation/Portrait
expect-rotation Portrait
tap-on Upside down/On
expect-rotation Portrait inverted
expect-setting rotation=180
tap-on Close
tilt upright
wait 1500
expect-rotation Portrait inverted
restart
expect-rotation Portrait inverted
tap-on Options
tap-on Upside down/Off
tap-on Orientation/Auto
tap-on Close
expect-rotation Portrait
